{
  "dom_id": "step-8701",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Calculating the Measure of a Line Segment Using a Ruler",
  "problem": "The ruler shown below allows measuring length both in $\\textrm{cm}$ (centimeters) and $\\textrm{in}$ (inches). Determine the measure of the line segment $\\overline{MN}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14150837/assets/e1d80c4344e4051f1b58a8c7ec1db9930f06d679c1a0532e83bfc7bdb719c4c1.png)",
  "worked_solution": "Note that $M$ is not aligned with the zero-mark on the ruler. \n\nTo find the length, we read the values that correspond to the points $M$ and $N,$ and take the difference.\n\nFrom the picture, we see that $M$ corresponds to $0.5\\,\\textrm{in}$ while $N$ corresponds to $2\\,\\textrm{in}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MN=2\\,\\text{in}-0.5\\,\\text{in}=1.5\\,\\text{in}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
